From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Piotr Oniszczuk <piotr.oniszczuk@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 11:21:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1889/1890] arm64: dts: amlogic: s7: add audio controllers

Add the audio controllers of the Amlogic S7 SoC: the audio clock
controller, the memory to/from DDR FIFOs, the TDM, SPDIF and PDM
interfaces and the HDMI transmitter glue (tohdmitx).

The audio block is the same as on S4. The vendor txhd2 audio clock
driver uses the SC2/S4 register layout, only the mclk parent 0 is
hifi1_pll instead of mpll0. S7 has no MPLL, so the mst_in1..3 inputs
of the clock controller are not connected.

The HDMI transmitter is the HDMI 2.1 one, like on T7, which needs the
master clock of the I2S source, so tohdmitx falls back to the T7
variant.

Signed-off-by: Piotr Oniszczuk <piotr.oniszczuk@gmail.com>
